 "notes": "Box: the regular Sunset grid south of Lincoln Way and west of Sunset Blvd (blocks 1706-1713, 1792-1799, 1809-1816, 1883-1890 and slivers of the blocks west of them), ordinary built-up ground with several zoning borders: RH-1/RH-2/NC-1 borders that run mostly through the middle of blocks (y ~1627-1634 in the 1710-1713 row, y ~1799-1805 in the 1792-1795 row, y ~1871-1877 in the 1809-1816 row, x ~1272-1279 in 1710 and 1795), wiggling NC-1 borders across the streets (x 905-1000, y 1800-1880; x 1200-1300, y 1620-1700), P boxes round 1797 and 1888 (x 1076-1083 / 1153-1162, in the avenues beside the block outlines), RH-2 boxes at 1713 and 1816, and the heavy line x 1549-1555 along the west side of Sunset Blvd at the right edge (the box ends in it, so the Sunset Blvd strip blocks with their curved ramp lines east of x 1556 are out). Every block has its own thin closed outline; borders through a block do not split it. Corners on the street-side edge of each thin line, read off 4x ruled close-ups and checked against dark-run profiles of page.png along rows and columns. Judgment calls (page px): (1) where heavy borders or lettering lie on a block's line (bottom of 1709/1710 under the NC-1 border at x 1200-1300, y 1620-1690; top of 1809 under 'NC-1' lettering and the NC-1 border at x 905-990, y 1830-1870; top of 1713 and 1816 at the RH-2 boxes; 'RH-1' lettering across 1886-1887 at y 2120-2145) the outline is typed straight through along the visible thin line on either side. (2) The x 905-913 strip at the left edge holds the east edges of the four blocks west of 1706/1799/1809/1890, typed as cut blocks.",
